# QA artifacts and locations

## Templates and references

- **Test case draft format (norms + schema template)**: [epics/templates/tests-ref.json](../../epics/templates/tests-ref.json) (**format_norms**); pipeline [`.cursor/pipelines/test-prep.md`](../pipelines/test-prep.md)
- **Defect report format reference**: [docs/dr-ref](docs/dr-ref)
- **Epic handoff template** (copy per Epic): [epics/templates/epic-ref.json](epics/templates/epic-ref.json) → durable file `epics/<KEY>/<KEY>-ref.json` — layout: [epics/README.md](epics/README.md); pipeline: [`.cursor/pipelines/epic-prep.md`](../pipelines/epic-prep.md) (**`client_shell_impact`**, **`snippet_status`** on requirements)
- **Epic coverage + Jira Smart Checklist norms**: [epics/templates/coverage-ref.json](epics/templates/coverage-ref.json) → `epics/<KEY>/<KEY>-coverage.json` + `<KEY>-coverage.md`; playbook: [`.cursor/pipelines/coverage.md`](../pipelines/coverage.md) (*Smart Checklist markdown*, `epic_verification_focus`, `verification_role`, **`checks[].calculation_contract`**, optional `focus=`)
- **Epic requirement analysis**: [epics/templates/analysis-ref.json](epics/templates/analysis-ref.json) → `epics/<KEY>/<KEY>-analysis.json` + `<KEY>-analysis.md`; playbook: [`.cursor/pipelines/analysis.md`](../pipelines/analysis.md) (**`ANALYSE:`**, Jira known issues, gaps/questions, optional **Known issue** **`>`** append to `-coverage` with dedupe)
- **Epic regression test drafts**: [epics/templates/tests-ref.json](epics/templates/tests-ref.json) → `epics/<KEY>/<KEY>-tests.json` + `<KEY>-tests.md`; playbook: [`.cursor/pipelines/test-prep.md`](../pipelines/test-prep.md) (**`TEST-PREP:`**, checklist traceability, Jira test search + fetch, optional **`map_only=yes`**)
- **Epic optional E2E materialization (Playwright + readonly DB)**: [epics/templates/test-exec-ref.json](epics/templates/test-exec-ref.json) → `epics/<KEY>/<KEY>-test-exec.json` + `epics/<KEY>/tests/*.spec.ts`; playbook: [`.cursor/pipelines/test-exec.md`](../pipelines/test-exec.md) (**`TEST-EXEC:`**, requires **`-tests.json`**; environment-dependent; temp under `epics/<KEY>/temp/` then delete)
- **Public scrub / export (release branch only)**: playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/public-scrub.md`](../pipelines/public-scrub.md) (**`PUBLIC-SCRUB:`**); durable on **`release`**: `docs/public-export-manifest.json`, optional `.agents/`; example manifest on internal branches: [docs/public-export-manifest.example.json](../../docs/public-export-manifest.example.json)
- **Harness SYNC (develop / main only)**: playbook [`.cursor/pipelines/sync.md`](../pipelines/sync.md) (**`SYNC:`**); reconciles router, harness-map, AGENTS, README, HOW-TO, this file, prompts, templates, tool docs per [harness-maintenance.mdc](harness-maintenance.mdc); ephemeral **`automation/temp/sync/`** then delete — **not** for **`release`**

Align new test case drafts with [epics/templates/tests-ref.json](../../epics/templates/tests-ref.json) / **dr-ref** unless the task defines a different format. Epic Smart Checklist drafts follow **coverage.md**. Epic regression bundles follow **test-prep.md** after coverage exists.

## Automation folder (`automation/`)

Manual **Python tests and tools** (not “workspace automation”). Tool docs: [automation/docs/](automation/docs/) (e.g. Yogi). Agent playbooks: [`.cursor/pipelines/`](../pipelines/).

- **Temporary / agent scratch**: [automation/temp/](automation/temp/) — short-lived only; promote outcomes to proper docs or handoff.

